# Sources used:
# - Rebel Up! Soundclash, Bouyon Hardcore post (opened 2026-10-20): bouyon hardcore and bouyon gwada context, and the passage stating that it took until December 2012 before the first Dominican and Guadeloupean MCs and DJs came to Paris, with a 50 minute documentary in French and Creole of the first performance in Paris of Suppa, Gaza Girls, Dj Joe and others. The same post describes bouyon gwada, heavy percussive riddims, and links a Marflix bouyon podcast from March 2013.
# - YouTube, Suppa feat Ti Cho Ghetto Princess "Never Stop Di Bouyon" (search result, 2026-10-20): description points to vadoreconcept.hautetfort.com and its keyword list includes Dj Joe, Vadore Concept, Gaza Crew, Gwada, Triple Kay and Asa Bantan. Used only as a scene and label proximity trace, not as a performance credit.
# - Shazam, DJ JOE "Bwé Rhum (feat. Asa Bantan) [Bouyon Kings Mixtape]" (2026-10-20): released February 5, 2023 by Vadore Concept Groupe as a single, BPM 157, credits list DJ JOE as performer, Foster XAVIER as songwriter, and a composer line that reads "Sesame Street's Little Boy", quoted here exactly as published as an example of unreliable platform metadata.
# - Shazam, Asa Bantan artist page (2026-10-20): lists both "Bwé Rhum (feat. DJ JOE)" under Asa Bantan and "Bwé Rhum (feat. Asa Bantan) [Bouyon Kings Mixtape]" under DJ JOE, plus a 2023 single entry "Bwé Rhum (feat. DJ JOE) - Single" under Asa Bantan releases.
# - Deezer and VirtualDJ community chart (2026-10-20): VirtualDJ lists "DJ JOE Bwé Rhum (Bouyon Kings Mixtape) (feat. Asa Bantan)", 2023, with the platform genre tag Cajun, a tagging error this profile notes and does not repeat as fact.
# - Disambiguation: DJ Joe is one of the most common DJ names in the world. No fact from any other DJ Joe, in house, hip hop, gospel, soca or any other scene, is used here. The Paris 2012 trace and the 2023 Vadore Concept single share the same Guadeloupe bouyon and Vadore circle, which is stated as proximity, not as a proven identity.
# Note: no source consulted establishes DJ Joe real name, origin, age or verified official accounts, so sameAs stays empty. Asa Bantan is described in site style as an artist widely called the King of Bouyon, attributed, never stated as a bare title of fact.

